CONFLICT_TEXT={
'c_core40_42_39':'Approximately 40 Å in the main prose, 42 Å ±10% in optical/SAXS labels, and 39 Å ±8.2% in TEM have distinct measurement definitions. Note 22 explicitly pairs 40 Å with 180 °C; it does not provide a separate 42 Å setting.',
'c_saxs5p3_5p6':'The highest Zn/Cd ratio in the independent solution-SAXS series is 5.3 in Figure 11 and p. 9, but 5.6 in the p. 8 Guinier discussion.',
'c_sigma':'Bare solution-SAXS polydispersity is approximately 0.12 in p. 9 prose and 0.11 in the Figure 12 caption.',
'c_high_saxs_fit':'Figure 12 labels sample d with σ = 0.25 even though the prose considers high-coverage mean size and variance unreliable. The caption fit is not proof of a reliable average.',
'c_F14_core':'Figure 14 calls the core 20 Å in diameter, while its surrounding text says approximately 20 Å in radius. The plotted radial boundary does not authorize silently correcting the caption.',
'c_CdS_core':'CdS Methods specify 33.5–35 Å core diameters; p. 11 says approximately 30 Å radius; Figure 16 and p. 12 say approximately 16 Å radius. The source does not resolve whether different specimens explain this.',
'c_F16_barrier':'Figure 16 describes 4/10 eV barriers into a surrounding CdS matrix. The model prose assigns those barriers to the organic matrix and gives 0.2/0.55 eV for CdS.',
'c_detector_distance':'The SAXS instrument description places the detector at D = 370 mm from the detector. The other endpoint is unresolved.',
'c_theta':'The WAXS simulation range is printed as 15° < θ < 60°, while the Figure 13 axis is 2θ. Approximate feature positions remain associated with the plotted axis.',
'c_model_aspect':'WAXS core-model aspect ratio is initially 1.1 and later 1.15; Table 1 gives a measured TEM mean of 1.12. These are not one exact shared value.',
'c_photo_color':'Figure 3 is described as a color photograph, but the supplied PDF reproduction is grayscale. Its colors have not been reconstructed.',
'c_nominal_actual':'Nominal geometric dose, actual WDS Zn/Cd, TEM-derived coverage and SAXS/WAXS fitted composition are different quantities. Deposited shell can be less than the precursor addition.',
'c_cds_storage_equal':'Equal hexane and butanol amounts for CdS storage lack an explicit mass/volume basis or absolute quantities.',
'c_monolayer_geometry':'The shell-monolayer convention is 3.1 Å along the major axis, whereas precursor-dose design assumes spherical geometry. Thick-shell particles are prolate and nonuniform.',
'c_oxidation_threshold':'Oxide absence is described at approximately 1.3 monolayers or more; unchanged Se/Cd after 80 h is stated for more than 1.3 monolayers. The 1.3/2.6-monolayer Auger parameters remain unchanged.',
'c_model_counterfactual':'Hypothetical 16/15 Å CdSe shells with 290/390 meV shifts are model comparisons, not additional experimentally synthesized products.',
'c_prior_film_devices':'The Introduction’s approximately 10% ES-OMCVD film yield and cathodoluminescence belong to reference 21. LED discussions cite reference 20 manuscripts; these are not new, fully specified experiments in this article.'}

def main():
    content();refs=references();identity=read(B/'source-identity.json');manifest=read(B/'crop-assets/manifest.json')
    assert manifest['source_sha256']==identity['main_sha256']
    assets={'figures':[],'tables':[],'equations':[],'schemes':[],'source_notes':[]};file_sources={}
    for a in manifest['assets']:
        ident=re.sub(r'^(figure|table|equation)-0',r'\1-',a['id']);p=B/'crop-assets'/a['relative_asset'];assert sha(p)==a['sha256'];links,cohorts=ASSET_LINKS[ident]
        assert a['visually_reviewed']
        kind='tables' if ident.startswith('table-') else 'equations' if ident.startswith(('equation-','formula-')) else 'source_notes' if ident.startswith('source-note-') else 'figures'
        v={'id':ident,'label':a['title'],'document_role':'main','page':a['pdf_page'],'printed_page':a['printed_page'],'source_locators':[loc(a['pdf_page'],a['title'])],'caption_paraphrase':a['caption_paraphrase'],'sample_scope':a['sample_scope'],'sample_links':[RECORDS[k] for k in links],'cohort_keys':cohorts,'sample_linkage':'Source-cohort context only; model-only items do not create synthesis outcomes or measured atomic structures.','formulation_labels':cohorts,'evidence_class':a['evidence_type'],'public_asset':'assets/figures/'+SID+'/'+a['relative_asset'],'public_asset_sha256':a['sha256'],'asset_provenance':{'source_file':'10.1021_jp971091y.pdf','source_sha256':identity['main_sha256'],'source_pdf_page':a['pdf_page'],'crop_bbox_pdf_points_top_left':a['bbox_pdf_points_top_left'],'crop_normalized':a['crop_normalized'],'render_dpi':a['dpi'],'pixel_dimensions':a['pixel_dimensions'],'renderer':a['renderer'],'transformation':'Original PDF raster crop; no curve digitization, synthetic coloring or replacement.'},'quantitative_context':a.get('quantitative_context',a.get('scope_caveats',[])),'notes':a.get('scope_caveats',[]),'text_reviewed':True,'visual_reviewed':True,'reviewed':False,'reader_render_verified':False,'training_eligible':False,'source_asset_type':a['type']}
        if a.get('panels'):v['panels']=a['panels']
        if ident=='table-1':v.update(structured_rows=TABLE_ROWS,data_role='Source table:measured TEM/WDS values and fitted SAXS/WAXS values remain separate; blank cells are null.')
